    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0446" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/476.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department of State acknowledges the receipt of the confidential memorandum
                    handed it to-day by the Mexican ambassador relative to the recruiting
                    [etc.].</p>
                <pb facs="0447" n="365" xml:id="pg365"/>
                <p>The Department of State begs to advise the ambassador of Mexico that a
                    translation of his memorandum has been communicated to the Secretary of War and
                    to the Attorney General for such action as they may deem appropriate.</p>
            </div>
